n-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Carter</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Karn</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Kreyling</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Lai</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Olin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Monteiro-Riviere</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Warheit</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Principles for characterising the potential human health effects from exposure to nanomaterials: Elements of a screening strategy. A report from the ILSI Research Foundation/Risk Science Institute</article-title><source>Particle &#x00026; Fibre Toxicol</source><year>2005</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>8</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1743-8977-2-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Forum Series</collab></person-group><article-title>Research Strategies for safety evaluation of nanomaterials. Parts I &#x02013; V</article-title><source>Toxicol Sci</source><year>2005</year><fpage>87</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16339789</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fallerl</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Barcher</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Dami</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Roguet</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Predictive ability of reconstructed human epidermis equivalents for the assessment of skin irritation of cosmetics</article-title><source>Toxicol in Vitro</source><year>2002</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>557</fpage><lpage>572</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12206823</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0887-2333(02)00053-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hartung</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Statement on the validity of in vitro tests for skin irritation</article-title><source>ECVAM</source><comment>27<sup>th </sup>April, 2007</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Health Effects Institute</collab></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of human risk from cerium added to diesel fuel</article-title><source>HEI</source><year>2001</year><comment>Communication 9</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Donaldson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Stone</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Clouter</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Renwick</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>MacNee</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ultrafine particles</article-title><source>Occup Environ Med</source><year>2001</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>211</fpage><lpage>216</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11171936</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/oem.58.3.211</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beck-Speier</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Dayal</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Karg</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Maier</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Schumann</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Schulz</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Semmler</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Takenaka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Stettmaier</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bors</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghio</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Samet</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Heyder</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Oxidative stress and lipid mediators induced in alveolar macrophages by ultrafine particles</article-title><source>Free Rad Biol Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>1080</fpage><lpage>1092</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15780766</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.freeradbiomed.2005.01.004</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>MacNee</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Stone</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Donaldson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Size dependent proinflammatory effects of ultrafine polystyrene particles: a role for surface area and oxidative stress in the enhanced activity of ultrafines</article-title><source>Toxicol appl Pharmacol</source><year>2001</year><volume>175</volume><fpage>191</fpage><lpage>199</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11559017</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/taap.2001.9240</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Scientific Committee on Emerging and Newly Identified Health Risks (SCENIHR)</collab></person-group><article-title>Opinion on &#x02013; The appropriateness of existing methodologies to asses the potential risks associated with engineered and adventitious products of nanotechnologies</article-title><comment>28&#x02013;29<sup>th </sup>Sept. 2005, SCENIHR/002/05</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>COT, COM COC</collab></person-group><article-title>Joint Statement on Nanomaterial Toxicology</article-title><year>2005</year></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>BS EN ISO 10993-5</collab></person-group><article-title>Biological evaluation of medical devices. Tests for in vitro cytotoxicity</article-title><year>1999</year></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maron</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ames</surname><given-names>BN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Revised methods for the Salmonella mutagenicity test</article-title><source>Mutat Research</source><year>1983</year><volume>113</volume><fpage>173</fpage><lpage>215</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kirkland</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><collab>Ed</collab></person-group><source>Statistical evaluation of mutagenicity test data UKEMS sub-committee on Guidelines for Mutagenicity testing</source><year>1989</year><publisher-name>Report Part III, Cambridge University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD)</collab></person-group><article-title><italic>Daphnia magna sp</italic>. Acute immobilisation test No. 202</article-title><source>Chemicals Testing Guidelines, Series 200</source><year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD) Environment Directorate</collab></person-group><article-title>Guidance Document on Aquatic Toxicity Testing of Difficult Substances and Mixtures</article-title><source>OECD Series on testing and Assessment Number 23</source><year>2000</year></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>European Centre for Ecotoxicology and Toxicology of Chemicals (ECETOC)</collab></person-group><article-title>Aquatic Toxicity Testing of Sparingly Soluble, Volatile and Unstable Substances</article-title><source>Monograph No 26</source><year>1996</year></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD) Environment Directorate, Chemicals Testing Guidelines, Series 200</collab></person-group><article-title>Activated Sludge, Respiration Inhibition Test No. 209</article-title><year>1984</year></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>